  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Unsupervised Learning: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unsupervised Learning: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Unsupervised== = find structure in **unlabelled** data",
                "Two jobs: {blue:clustering} and {purple:dimensionality reduction}",
                "No ground truth: judge by ==internal metrics== and usefulness, not accuracy",
                "Distance-based, so ==large-scale features dominate== unless standardised"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rows vs Columns",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Clustering",
                "Dim. reduction"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Groups",
                  "**rows**",
                  "**columns**"
                ],
                [
                  "Output",
                  "labels",
                  "fewer features"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "k-means",
                  "PCA"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The two are often ==chained==: PCA, then k-means"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "make_pipeline(",
                "    StandardScaler(),",
                "    PCA(n_components=0.95),",
                "    KMeans(n_clusters=4, n_init=10))"
              ],
              "note": "scale, compress, cluster"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Core Workflow",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Scale",
                    "sub": "standardise",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pick method",
                    "sub": "fits the shape",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Tune",
                    "sub": "k, eps, components",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Validate",
                    "sub": "metric + profiles",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Validate twice",
              "text": "A good metric is not enough. Also read the ==cluster profiles==: do the groups make sense?"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why no accuracy?** There are no labels, so use silhouette and cluster profiles",
                "**Why scale first?** Distances let big-scale features dominate"
              ],
              "style": "star",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "k-means and Choosing k",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "k-means and Choosing k",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The k-means Loop",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Place k centroids",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Assign",
                    "sub": "nearest centroid",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Move",
                    "sub": "to cluster mean",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repeat",
                    "sub": "until labels stop changing",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Minimises ==inertia== = within-cluster sum of squares",
                "`n_init` = number of random restarts; the best inertia is kept",
                "==k-means++== spreads the starting centroids"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choosing k",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Look at",
                "Pick"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Elbow",
                  "inertia vs k; always falls as k grows",
                  "the {blue:bend}, where gains shrink; never the minimum"
                ],
                [
                  "Silhouette",
                  "score from -1 to 1; higher = tighter, better separated",
                  "k with the ==highest average=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. In sklearn",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fit on scaled data, then read the fitted attributes",
                "`labels_`, `cluster_centers_`, `inertia_`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "km = KMeans(n_clusters=4, n_init=10,",
                "            random_state=0).fit(X_scaled)",
                "km.labels_           # cluster per row",
                "km.cluster_centers_  # one centroid each",
                "km.inertia_          # within-cluster SSE"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Not scaling: large-scale features dominate distance",
                "Assuming round, equal-sized clusters",
                "Trusting one random start: use k-means++ and several `n_init`",
                "Running it on categorical data: means are meaningless"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hierarchical Clustering and DBSCAN",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Hierarchical Clustering and DBSCAN",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Agglomerative and the Dendrogram",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Every point starts as ==its own cluster==",
                "Repeatedly ==merge the closest pair==; the tree is a **dendrogram**",
                "Cut ==horizontally== at a height to get the clusters",
                "A ==long vertical gap== before a merge suggests a natural number of clusters"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "n clusters",
                    "sub": "one per point",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Merge",
                    "sub": "closest pair",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repeat",
                    "sub": "until one",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Dendrogram",
                    "sub": "cut at a height",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Linkage: what 'closest' means",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Linkage",
                "Distance",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`single`",
                  "nearest pair",
                  "chaining, elongated"
                ],
                [
                  "`complete`",
                  "farthest pair",
                  "compact"
                ],
                [
                  "`average`",
                  "mean of pairs",
                  "compromise"
                ],
                [
                  "`ward`",
                  "least variance increase",
                  "==usual default=="
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. DBSCAN",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==eps== = neighbourhood radius; ==min_samples== = density threshold",
                "{green:Core}: at least min_samples neighbours within eps",
                "{blue:Border}: sits near a core point",
                "{red:Noise}: everything else, labelled ==-1=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from sklearn.cluster import DBSCAN",
                "db = DBSCAN(eps=0.5, min_samples=5)",
                "db.fit(X_scaled)",
                "db.labels_  # -1 = noise"
              ],
              "note": "no n_clusters argument"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Pro}: no k needed; arbitrary shapes plus outliers",
                "{red:Con}: struggles with varying densities",
                "{red:Con}: hierarchical costs ==O(n²)== memory, so not for large data"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Choosing eps",
              "text": "Plot sorted k-distances and take the ==elbow== as eps."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "PCA and Explained Variance",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "PCA and Explained Variance",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What PCA Does",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "PCA projects data onto ==orthogonal axes== (principal components)",
                "Axes ordered by ==variance captured==, PC1 largest",
                "A {blue:linear} method"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Centre",
                    "sub": "subtract mean",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Covariance",
                    "sub": "of features",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Eigenvectors",
                    "sub": "or SVD",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Project",
                    "sub": "onto top PCs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Components = ==eigenvectors==",
                "Explained variance = matching ==eigenvalue=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choosing Components",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`explained_variance_ratio_` = each component's share",
                "Keep components until the cumulative share hits ==95%==, or pass `n_components=0.95`",
                "==Standardise== first, or large-scale features dominate",
                "Fit on ==train only==, then `transform` the test set"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "sc = StandardScaler().fit(X_train)",
                "pca = PCA(n_components=0.95)",
                "Z_train = pca.fit_transform(sc.transform(X_train))",
                "Z_test = pca.transform(sc.transform(X_test))"
              ],
              "note": "scaler and PCA both learn from train only"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Limits",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Components are linear mixes of features: hard to interpret",
                "Misses non-linear structure",
                "Sensitive to outliers"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Order matters",
              "text": "==Scale first==, then PCA. Fitting either on test data leaks information."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "t-SNE and UMAP for Visualisation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "t-SNE and UMAP for Visualisation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What They Do",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Non-linear== methods that squash data to **2D or 3D**",
                "They preserve ==local neighbourhoods==",
                "t-SNE knob: ==perplexity== (about 5-50) = effective neighbour count",
                "Try several perplexities: the picture changes"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "t-SNE",
                "UMAP"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "slower",
                  "{green:faster}, scales better"
                ],
                [
                  "Global structure",
                  "weak",
                  "keeps **more**"
                ],
                [
                  "New points",
                  "no",
                  "{green:`transform`}"
                ],
                [
                  "Knobs",
                  "`perplexity`",
                  "`n_neighbors`, `min_dist`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reading the Plot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "t-SNE cluster ==distances== mean nothing",
                "t-SNE cluster ==sizes== mean nothing",
                "A plot is not proof of clusters",
                "Do not feed the embedding to a model"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "Z = PCA(50).fit_transform(X_scaled)",
                "TSNE(perplexity=30, random_state=0).fit_transform(Z)",
                "umap.UMAP(n_neighbors=15, min_dist=0.1,",
                "          random_state=0).fit_transform(Z)"
              ],
              "note": "PCA to ~50 dims first for speed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Plots only",
              "items": [
                "Set ==random_state== to reproduce",
                "PCA to ~50 dims first",
                "Vary perplexity / n_neighbors"
              ],
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Visualise with them. ==Never read gaps or sizes== as real separation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unsupervised Methods Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unsupervised Methods Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pick by Need",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Pick"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Round clusters, large data",
                  "{blue:k-means}"
                ],
                [
                  "Dendrogram, small data",
                  "{purple:Hierarchical}"
                ],
                [
                  "Odd shapes plus noise",
                  "{orange:DBSCAN}"
                ],
                [
                  "Compress features",
                  "{green:PCA}"
                ],
                [
                  "Visualise in 2D",
                  "{pink:t-SNE / UMAP}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Unsupervised or Supervised?",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Labels ==missing or costly==: unsupervised",
                "Jobs: segmentation, anomaly detection, feature compression, exploration",
                "Labels **and** a target: supervised"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Metrics and Rules",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Metric"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "k-means",
                  "inertia + elbow"
                ],
                [
                  "Any clustering",
                  "==silhouette=="
                ],
                [
                  "PCA",
                  "cumulative `explained_variance_ratio_`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Always ==scale== first",
                "Fit transformers on the **training set** only",
                "Fix `random_state`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Quick Calls",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "KMeans(n_clusters=k, n_init=10)",
                "AgglomerativeClustering(linkage='ward')",
                "DBSCAN(eps=0.5, min_samples=5)",
                "PCA(n_components=0.95)",
                "TSNE(perplexity=30)",
                "umap.UMAP()"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Scale first",
              "text": "Unscaled features break distance-based methods and PCA. ==Scale, then fit.=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You run k-means for k=1 to 10 and pick the k with the lowest inertia. What went wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Inertia always falls as k grows, so the minimum is k=10 (or k=n, where it reaches 0).",
                "Pick the elbow, or the k with the highest silhouette."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "DBSCAN returns labels [0, 0, 1, 1, -1, 0]. How many clusters are there?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Two: 0 and 1.",
                "-1 marks noise, not a cluster."
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "labels = [0, 0, 1, 1, -1, 0]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "PCA on raw age (0-100) and income (0-100000) gives PC1 a ratio near 0.99. Why is this misleading?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Income's huge scale dominates the variance, so PC1 is basically income.",
                "Standardise first, then PCA."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
